---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
---

<Layout
  title="Fantasy Football World Cup — Draft & Simulate | World Cup Simulator"
  description="Build your fantasy World Cup dream team from 100+ historical squads (1970-2026), then watch them face the all-time greats in a simulated knockout tournament. Free browser game, no download."
>
  <main class="min-h-screen bg-canvas text-white">
    <section class="relative overflow-hidden">
      <div
        class="pointer-events-none absolute -top-48 left-1/2 h-96 w-2xl -translate-x-1/2 rounded-full bg-mint/15 blur-[120px]"
      >
      </div>
      <div
        class="pointer-events-none absolute top-24 -left-32 h-64 w-64 rounded-full bg-uv/20 blur-[100px]"
      >
      </div>

      <div
        class="relative mx-auto max-w-5xl px-4 pt-16 pb-12 text-center sm:px-6 sm:pt-24 sm:pb-16"
      >
        <p
          class="font-mono text-[11px] font-semibold tracking-[1.8px] text-mint uppercase"
        >
          World Cup Draft Simulator
        </p>
        <h1
          class="mt-4 font-display text-6xl leading-[0.85] tracking-[1.07px] text-balance text-mint sm:text-7xl md:text-8xl"
        >
          Fantasy Football World Cup: Simulate the World Cup
        </h1>
      <p class="mx-auto mt-6 max-w-2xl text-secondary">
        World Cup Draft Simulator is a free browser soccer game and the
        fantasy football world cup experience: draft a dream XI from 100+
        historical squads — Brazil 1970, France 1998, Argentina 2022 — and run
        it through a simulated group stage, knockout bracket and penalty
        shootouts. It's a soccer simulator, football draft simulator and world
        cup fantasy game you play online with no download and no sign-up. In the
        US it's a soccer draft game, online soccer game and free soccer
        simulation game; elsewhere the fantasy soccer draft and interactive
        soccer simulator of choice. The world cup simulator 2026 mode adds fresh
        predicted squads so you can predict your own tournament today. Pick a
        formation, build your squad, and let the match engine simulate the cup.
      </p>

        <div class="mt-8 flex flex-wrap items-center justify-center gap-3">
          <a
            href="/game"
            class="rounded-full bg-mint px-8 py-3 font-mono text-[11px] font-semibold tracking-[1.8px] text-black uppercase transition-colors duration-150 hover:bg-white"
          >
            Start drafting
          </a>
          <a
            href="/how-to-play"
            class="rounded-full border border-white/15 px-8 py-3 font-mono text-[11px] font-semibold tracking-[1.8px] text-white uppercase transition-colors duration-150 hover:border-mint hover:text-mint"
          >
            How to play
          </a>
        </div>

        <ul class="mt-10 flex flex-wrap items-center justify-center gap-2">
          {
            [
              "1970-2026",
              "100+ squads",
              "12 draft rounds",
              "Group → knockout",
              "Penalty shootouts",
            ].map((s) => (
              <li class="rounded-full border border-white/15 bg-slate/40 px-4 py-1.5 font-mono text-[10px] font-semibold tracking-[1.5px] text-secondary uppercase">
                {s}
              </li>
            ))
          }
        </ul>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="border-t border-white/10 bg-slate/20">
      <div class="mx-auto max-w-5xl px-4 py-14 sm:px-6 sm:py-20">
        <p
          class="text-center font-mono text-[11px] font-semibold tracking-[1.8px] text-mint uppercase"
        >
          How it works
        </p>
        <h2
          class="mt-3 text-center font-display text-4xl leading-[0.9] tracking-[0.5px] sm:text-5xl"
        >
          Four rounds to glory
        </h2>
        <ol class="mt-10 grid gap-4 sm:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-4">
          <li
            class="flex flex-col rounded-2xl border border-white/10 bg-slate/40 p-5"
          >
            <span class="flex items-center justify-between">
              <span
                class="font-mono text-[10px] font-semibold tracking-[1.5px] text-mint"
                >01</span
              >
            </span>
            <span class="mt-4 block font-display text-xl tracking-[0.5px]"
              >Pick your shape</span
            >
            <span class="mt-2 block text-xs leading-relaxed text-secondary">
              Choose from 4-3-3, 4-4-2, 3-5-2 or 4-2-3-1. This locks the slot
              limits for all 12 draft rounds.
            </span>
          </li>
          <li
            class="flex flex-col rounded-2xl border border-white/10 bg-slate/40 p-5"
          >
            <span class="flex items-center justify-between">
              <span
                class="font-mono text-[10px] font-semibold tracking-[1.5px] text-mint"
                >02</span
              >
            </span>
            <span class="mt-4 block font-display text-xl tracking-[0.5px]"
              >Draft your XI</span
            >
            <span class="mt-2 block text-xs leading-relaxed text-secondary">
              Twelve rounds of picks from 100+ historical World Cup squads.
              Chase stars, patch gaps, keep one on the bench.
            </span>
          </li>
          <li
            class="flex flex-col rounded-2xl border border-white/10 bg-slate/40 p-5"
          >
            <span class="flex items-center justify-between">
              <span
                class="font-mono text-[10px] font-semibold tracking-[1.5px] text-mint"
                >03</span
              >
            </span>
            <span class="mt-4 block font-display text-xl tracking-[0.5px]"
              >Auto-run the cup</span
            >
            <span class="mt-2 block text-xs leading-relaxed text-secondary">
              Your tournament simulates itself — group stage, knockout bracket,
              extra time and penalty shootouts.
            </span>
          </li>
          <li
            class="flex flex-col rounded-2xl border border-white/10 bg-slate/40 p-5"
          >
            <span class="flex items-center justify-between">
              <span
                class="font-mono text-[10px] font-semibold tracking-[1.5px] text-mint"
                >04</span
              >
            </span>
            <span class="mt-4 block font-display text-xl tracking-[0.5px]"
              >Replay &amp; results</span
            >
            <span class="mt-2 block text-xs leading-relaxed text-secondary">
              Rewatch goals, compare squad stats, and lift the trophy when it's
              all over.
            </span>
          </li>
      </ol>

      <div class="mx-auto mt-10 max-w-3xl text-sm leading-relaxed text-secondary">
        <p>
          World Cup Draft Simulator is built around one simple loop that makes
          it the most replayable fantasy football world cup game on the web. It
          begins when you pick your formation — choose 4-3-3 if you want width
          and attack, 4-4-2 for balance, 3-5-2 to own the midfield, or 4-2-3-1
          for control — and that single decision locks the defender,
          midfielder and attacker slots you must fill across the twelve draft
          rounds. From there the football draft simulator hands you a rolling
          board of historical World Cup squads and you build your dream XI one
          pick at a time, chasing elite talents, patching gaps, and banking one
          player on the bench for later. Once your squad is set, the soccer
          simulator takes over: your team joins a round-robin group with three
          AI opponents drawn from the same pool of semifinalists, and every
          group match is played out segment by segment by the match engine,
          with possession, shots, shot quality, expected goals and momentum all
          factored in. The knockout bracket then resolves itself automatically
          — round of 16, quarter-final, semi-final and final — so you can watch
          your tournament simulate from the first whistle to the trophy lift.
          Ties in the bracket go to extra time and, when needed, a penalty
          shootout simulator decides who advances, five kicks each before
          sudden death. Because the whole world cup simulation is generated
          inside the app, no two runs are the same: a Brazil 1970 front line
          can be undone by a disciplined Germany 2014 back line, and a long-shot
          draft can topple the seedings. That is why players call it both a
          soccer draft game and a world cup predictor — you are not predicting
          real results, you are predicting the cup you built. When the final
          whistle blows you can replay any match, compare squad stats and
          player ratings, and start a fresh draft to chase a better outcome. It
          is a free soccer simulation game that runs entirely in the browser,
          on any device, with no download and no sign-up, which is exactly what
          makes it an easy online soccer game to pick up between matches or on a
          phone. Whether you describe it as an interactive soccer simulator, a
          fantasy soccer draft, or simply the world cup fantasy game, the four
          rounds to glory stay the same: shape, draft, simulate, repeat.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

    <section class="border-t border-white/10">
      <div class="mx-auto max-w-5xl px-4 py-14 sm:px-6 sm:py-20">
        <p
          class="text-center font-mono text-[11px] font-semibold tracking-[1.8px] text-mint uppercase"
        >
          The squads
        </p>
        <h2
          class="mt-3 text-center font-display text-4xl leading-[0.9] tracking-[0.5px] sm:text-5xl"
        >
          Every World Cup great, one pool
        </h2>
        <p class="mx-auto mt-4 max-w-2xl text-center text-secondary">
          Draft from the semifinalists of every World Cup from 1970 to 2026.
          Browse the full squad pages with player ratings, then take them into
          the draft.
        </p>
        <div class="mt-10 flex flex-wrap items-center justify-center gap-3">
        <a
          href="/teams"
          class="rounded-full border border-white/15 px-8 py-3 font-mono text-[11px] font-semibold tracking-[1.8px] text-white uppercase transition-colors duration-150 hover:border-mint hover:text-mint"
        >
          Browse all squads
        </a>
        <a
          href="/game"
          class="rounded-full bg-mint px-8 py-3 font-mono text-[11px] font-semibold tracking-[1.8px] text-black uppercase transition-colors duration-150 hover:bg-white"
        >
          Play now
        </a>
      </div>

      <div class="mx-auto mt-10 max-w-3xl text-sm leading-relaxed text-secondary">
        <p>
          The squads are the heart of World Cup Draft Simulator, and they are
          what separate this football simulator from a generic bracket tool.
          Every team in the pool is a real World Cup semifinalist from 1970 to
          2026, rated on the same game-specific scale so your draft and the AI
          opponents are always compared fairly. That means the world cup
          winners, top scorers and best players of five decades are all sitting
          in the draft board waiting for you to pick them — Brazil 1970 and
          their fluid attacking empire, Netherlands 1974 with total football,
          Argentina 1978, Italy 1982, France 1982, West Germany across the
          eighties, Argentina 1986 and the genius of Maradona, Italy 1990,
          Brazil 1994, France 1998 and Zidane's midfield, Brazil 2002 and the
          three R's, Germany 2002, Italy 2006, Spain 2010 and tiki-taka,
          Germany 2014 and a relentless machine, France 2018, and Messi's
          Argentina 2022. Each squad arrives with player ratings across
          reflexes, tackling, passing, finishing, pace and vision, and those
          ratings drive the world cup simulation when matches play out. Drafting
          same-nation players triggers a chemistry boost, so rebuilding the best
          world cup team of all time is rewarded — stack Brazil 1970 or Argentina
          2022 and the engine notices cohesion. You can browse every roster on
          the teams page before you draft, study the average rating and the
          standout player, then carry that knowledge into the soccer draft game.
          Because the squads are the content, the app doubles as a museum of
          greatest world cup teams you can actually put on the pitch: pit
          Maradona's Argentina against Messi's, or Brazil 1970 against France
          2022, all generated inside the simulator rather than argued about
          online. The 2026 rosters are predicted lineups, not official
          selections, and every rating is tuned for balance rather than claimed
          as fact, which keeps the fantasy soccer draft honest and the matches
          close. In short, the squad pool is why this is a world cup fantasy
          game worth replaying — there is always one more all-time great to
          build around, and one more draft where the bench player becomes the
          hero.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

    <section class="border-t border-white/10">
      <div class="mx-auto max-w-5xl px-4 py-14 sm:px-6 sm:py-20">
        <p
          class="text-center font-mono text-[11px] font-semibold tracking-[1.8px] text-mint uppercase"
        >
          How to play
        </p>
        <h2
          class="mt-3 text-center font-display text-4xl leading-[0.9] tracking-[0.5px] sm:text-5xl"
        >
          Your world cup simulator, step by step
        </h2>
        <p class="mx-auto mt-4 max-w-2xl text-center text-secondary">
          World Cup Draft Simulator is an interactive soccer simulator that
          turns drafting into a full tournament. Choose a formation, draft your
          dream XI from 100+ historical squads, then watch the engine simulate
          every match — group stage, knockout bracket, extra time and penalty
          shootouts — and predict your own cup. It's a free soccer simulation
          game you can play right in the browser, on any device.
        </p>
        <div class="mt-10 flex flex-wrap items-center justify-center gap-3">
        <a
          href="/how-to-play"
          class="rounded-full border border-white/15 px-8 py-3 font-mono text-[11px] font-semibold tracking-[1.8px] text-white uppercase transition-colors duration-150 hover:border-mint hover:text-mint"
        >
          Full guide
        </a>
        <a
          href="/game"
          class="rounded-full bg-mint px-8 py-3 font-mono text-[11px] font-semibold tracking-[1.8px] text-black uppercase transition-colors duration-150 hover:bg-white"
        >
          Start drafting
        </a>
      </div>

      <div class="mx-auto mt-10 max-w-3xl text-sm leading-relaxed text-secondary">
        <p>
          Your world cup simulator is easier to start than it looks, and that is
          the point of an online soccer game built for the browser. Open the app
          and you are one click from a draft: no install, no account, no waiting.
          The first decision is your formation, and because the soccer simulator
          respects positions, the shape you choose decides how many defenders,
          midfielders and attackers you can take across the twelve rounds. From
          there the football draft simulator serves a rotating set of
          nation-and-year offers — Brazil 1970 one pick, Germany 2014 the next —
          and you place each player into a best-position slot, watch chemistry
          update, and use a small number of rerolls when the board is unkind.
          When the XI is complete the match engine simulates your group stage
          live, segment by segment, while the rest of the bracket is
          pre-simulated so the whole world cup simulation resolves in moments.
          Knockout ties that stay level after extra time fall to a penalty
          shootout simulator, five kicks each and then sudden death, exactly the
          drama every fan remembers. You are not predicting the real 2026
          results — you are using the world cup simulator 2026 mode to predict
          the tournament you assembled, which is why players also describe it as
          a world cup predictor for their own cup. It is a free soccer
          simulation game and a soccer game no download, so it runs on a laptop,
          tablet or phone without touching storage beyond your save. If you want
          the long version, the how-to-play guide walks through formations,
          drafting, chemistry and the bracket step by step, and the FAQ covers
          how the football simulation decides matches and how penalty shootouts
          work. However you frame it — fantasy soccer, interactive soccer
          simulator, or simply the world cup fantasy game — the path is the same:
          open the browser soccer game, draft your dream XI, and simulate the
          cup. The faster you start, the sooner your custom tournament is lifting
          a trophy you designed yourself.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</main>
</Layout>
